---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Nav from "../components/Nav.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";

const title = "About — AnySpace";
const description =
  "Why AnySpace exists, what we believe, and who builds it.";
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <Nav />
  <main id="main">
    <!-- Hero -->
    <section class="pt-28 pb-20 sm:pt-36 sm:pb-24">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl text-center">
          <p class="eyebrow mb-5">About</p>
          <h1 class="text-display text-fg">
            A workspace for the people
            <span class="text-fg-muted">orchestrating the agents.</span>
          </h1>
          <p class="mx-auto mt-7 max-w-2xl text-balance text-lg text-fg-muted sm:text-xl">
            Software gets built faster when humans direct, agents execute, and
            the workspace gets out of the way. AnySpace is that workspace.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Why we exist -->
    <section class="border-t border-border py-24 sm:py-28">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
          <p class="eyebrow mb-5">Why</p>
          <h2 class="text-display text-fg">
            The shell didn't get worse.
            <span class="text-fg-muted">The work around it did.</span>
          </h2>
          <div class="mt-10 space-y-5 text-base leading-relaxed text-fg-muted sm:text-lg">
            <p>
              We kept ending up with the same setup: a terminal in one window,
              an editor in another, a browser preview in a third, an AI chat in
              a fourth, a notes file somewhere on disk, and a Kanban board in
              the browser. Each tool was fine. The seams between them were the
              problem — and the seams kept multiplying as AI agents joined the
              loop.
            </p>
            <p>
              AnySpace is the answer to that. One window. Real PTYs, a real
              editor, a real browser preview, voice input, AI agents you
              actually control, and a Kanban board that <em>launches</em> the
              work instead of just describing it. Bring any CLI agent — Claude
              Code, Codex, Gemini, Aider, or your own — into a pane and
              orchestrate from there.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Principles -->
    <section class="border-t border-border py-24 sm:py-32">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl text-center">
          <p class="eyebrow mb-5">What we believe</p>
          <h2 class="text-display text-fg">
            Three rules we don't
            <span class="text-fg-muted">break.</span>
          </h2>
        </div>

        <div class="mx-auto mt-16 grid max-w-5xl grid-cols-1 gap-3 lg:grid-cols-3">
          <div class="rounded-xl border border-border bg-bg-elev/40 p-8 sm:p-10">
            <div class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-fg-muted">
              01 — Local-first
            </div>
            <h3 class="mt-3 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-fg">
              Your work stays on your machine.
            </h3>
            <p class="mt-4 text-base text-fg-muted">
              Settings, tasks, terminal scrollback, team coordination files —
              all on disk, in your tree. The network only sees what you
              explicitly send to an AI provider. See{" "}
              <a
                href="/docs/reference/privacy"
                class="underline decoration-border-strong underline-offset-[3px] transition-colors hover:decoration-fg"
                >the data-handling doc</a
              >{" "}
              for the file-by-file inventory.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="rounded-xl border border-border bg-bg-elev/40 p-8 sm:p-10">
            <div class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-fg-muted">
              02 — Bring your own keys
            </div>
            <h3 class="mt-3 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-fg">
              You choose the model. Every time.
            </h3>
            <p class="mt-4 text-base text-fg-muted">
              OpenAI, Anthropic, Groq, ElevenLabs, a local llama.cpp — same UI,
              same workspace. Our managed Cloud is convenience, not lock-in.
              Switch endpoints from Settings; nothing in the app cares which.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="rounded-xl border border-border bg-bg-elev/40 p-8 sm:p-10">
            <div class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-fg-muted">
              03 — Type less
            </div>
            <h3 class="mt-3 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-fg">
              The fastest input is the one you don't make.
            </h3>
            <p class="mt-4 text-base text-fg-muted">
              Hold-to-talk dictation, command blocks that <em>know</em> what
              ran, Super Brain that drafts the next command from context, and
              Team mode where multiple agents coordinate over plain files. The
              UI gets out of the way of the work.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- What it is, concretely -->
    <section class="border-t border-border py-24 sm:py-28">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
          <p class="eyebrow mb-5">What it is</p>
          <h2 class="text-display text-fg">
            A real desktop app.
            <span class="text-fg-muted">Not a browser tab.</span>
          </h2>
          <div class="mt-10 space-y-5 text-base leading-relaxed text-fg-muted sm:text-lg">
            <p>
              AnySpace is a native desktop application for macOS, Windows, and
              Linux, built on Tauri (Rust core, web frontend). Terminals are
              real PTYs — bash, zsh, anything you can <code>$PATH</code> to —
              not a transpiled shell-in-a-box. Editors are Monaco. Previews are
              an iframe pointed at your dev server. Mobile mirroring uses
              <code>scrcpy</code> for Android and Apple's ScreenCaptureKit for
              iOS Simulator.
            </p>
            <p>
              Underneath is a recursive split/leaf layout, an OSC-133-aware
              terminal that gives you Warp-style command blocks without
              hijacking your input, and a multi-agent coordination layer
              (Team mode) where agents talk through a shared{" "}
              <code>BOARD.md</code> and <code>MESSAGES.md</code> in your
              project tree. Boring, durable mechanisms — not magic.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Who -->
    <section class="border-t border-border py-24 sm:py-28">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
          <p class="eyebrow mb-5">Who</p>
          <h2 class="text-display text-fg">
            Built by
            <span class="text-fg-muted">Rebase LLC.</span>
          </h2>
          <div class="mt-10 space-y-5 text-base leading-relaxed text-fg-muted sm:text-lg">
            <p>
              A small team of builders who got tired of the seams. We use
              AnySpace to build AnySpace. If the workspace breaks our flow,
              we feel it the same day you do.
            </p>
            <p>
              Talk to us at{" "}
              <a
                href="mailto:support@anyspace.dev"
                class="underline decoration-border-strong underline-offset-[3px] transition-colors hover:decoration-fg"
                >support@anyspace.dev</a
              >, or open an issue on{" "}
              <a
                href="https://github.com/anyspacedev/anyspace"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener"
                class="underline decoration-border-strong underline-offset-[3px] transition-colors hover:decoration-fg"
                >GitHub</a
              >.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- CTA -->
    <section class="border-t border-border py-24 sm:py-28">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl text-center">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-fg sm:text-3xl">
            See it run.
          </h2>
          <p class="mx-auto mt-4 max-w-xl text-base text-fg-muted sm:text-lg">
            The fastest way to understand AnySpace is to spend ten minutes in
            it.
          </p>
          <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-3">
            <a
              href="/#download"
              class="inline-flex h-12 items-center justify-center gap-2 rounded-lg bg-fg px-6 font-medium text-bg transition-colors duration-fast ease-out hover:bg-fg/90 focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-ring focus-visible:ring-offset-2 focus-visible:ring-offset-bg"
            >
              Download
            </a>
            <a
              href="/docs"
              class="inline-flex h-12 items-center justify-center gap-2 rounded-lg border border-border-strong bg-transparent px-6 font-medium text-fg transition-colors duration-fast ease-out hover:bg-bg-elev focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-ring focus-visible:ring-offset-2 focus-visible:ring-offset-bg"
            >
              Read the docs
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>
